# S1.2 (PLAN.md, acceptance scenarios): the same kernel compiled at sm_89
# (its PTX body is the sm_80 fixture's; only .target differs) gives the
# same design point: the counts depend on the PTX, not on the target
# directive. The tile loop runs ⌈param_2/8⌉ trips, each 1024 f32 FLOPs
# and 32 global bytes loaded per thread.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/k5/k5.sm_89.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry _Z20hgemm_2d_blocktilingILi64ELi64ELi8ELi8ELi8EEviiifPK6__halfS2_fPS0_( // shared memory 2,048 B/CTA | per thread: flops f32 (1024·⌈param_2/8⌉ + 192); global load (32·⌈param_2/8⌉ + 128) B, store 128 B; shared load 256·⌈param_2/8⌉ B, store 32·⌈param_2/8⌉ B; param load 40 B{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}$L__BB0_2: // loop: trips ⌈param_2/8⌉ | under line 64 | exec ⌈param_2/8⌉/thread{{$}}
